# Modem

The modem talks QMI. These cells use the QMI client that `ExLocation`
starts at boot, so they work with or without cellular data configured.

```elixir
qmi = ExLocation.QMI
```

## Modem identity

```elixir
QMI.DeviceManagement.get_serial_numbers(qmi)
```

`imei` is the modem's IMEI.

```elixir
QMI.DeviceManagement.get_operating_mode(qmi)
```

## Network

These need a SIM card.

```elixir
QMI.NetworkAccess.get_home_network(qmi)
```

```elixir
QMI.NetworkAccess.get_signal_strength(qmi)
```

`rssi` is in dBm; closer to 0 is stronger.

## Mobile data

Mobile data is only set up when the firmware was built with the SIM's
APN (`FP3_APN=...`). Then the connection shows up as `rmnet0`:

```elixir
VintageNet.get(["interface", "rmnet0", "connection"])
```

`:internet` means the phone is online over the modem.
